\section{Purpose of This Document}
This README serves as the root-level publication guide for compiling,
maintaining, and distributing the ASTRO-SIM V1.0 monograph. It defines the
directory structure, build workflow, provenance sealing, and chapter
integration required to produce a complete, enterprise-grade scientific
volume.

\section{Directory Structure}
The monograph repository is organized as follows:

\begin{verbatim}
astro-sim-monograph/
│
├── chapters/
│   ├── chapter_introduction.tex
│   ├── chapter_architecture.tex
│   ├── chapter_operations_reliability.tex
│   ├── chapter_zero_trust.tex
│   ├── chapter_formal_verification.tex
│   └── ...
│
├── appendices/
│   ├── appendix_mathematics.tex
│   ├── appendix_cryptography.tex
│   └── appendix_distributed_systems.tex
│
├── assets/
│   └── listings/ (code samples, scripts)
│
├── build/
│   └── output PDFs and logs
│
└── monograph.tex (root compilation file)
\end{verbatim}

\section{Compilation Workflow}
The monograph is compiled using a two-pass \texttt{pdflatex} workflow to ensure
proper resolution of references, tables, and cross-links.

\begin{verbatim}
pdflatex monograph.tex
pdflatex monograph.tex
\end{verbatim}

For automated builds, a Makefile may be used:

\begin{verbatim}
make all
make clean
\end{verbatim}

\section{Chapter Integration}
The root file \texttt{monograph.tex} includes each chapter in sequence:

\begin{verbatim}
\include{chapters/chapter_introduction}
\include{chapters/chapter_architecture}
\include{chapters/chapter_operations_reliability}
\include{chapters/chapter_zero_trust}
\include{chapters/chapter_formal_verification}
\end{verbatim}

Appendices are included after the main body:

\begin{verbatim}
\appendix
\include{appendices/appendix_mathematics}
\include{appendices/appendix_cryptography}
\end{verbatim}

\section{Provenance Sealing}
All compiled PDFs are sealed using SHA-3/256 hashing:

\begin{verbatim}
sha3sum build/astro-sim-monograph.pdf > build/ledger.txt
\end{verbatim}

The ledger is signed using an HSM-backed key:

\begin{verbatim}
astro-cli sign --file build/ledger.txt --hsm-key CMB-AUTH-KEY-V1
\end{verbatim}

\section{Versioning Guidelines}
Monograph versions follow semantic versioning:

\begin{verbatim}
v1.0.0  Initial publication
v1.1.0  Added Operations & Reliability chapter
v1.2.0  Added Zero-Trust Hardening chapter
v1.3.0  Added Formal Verification appendix
\end{verbatim}

\section{Distribution Policy}
The monograph may be distributed in the following formats:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Internal enterprise documentation
    \item Academic submission (PDF)
    \item HPC lab technical reference
    \item Cryptographically sealed archival copy
\end{itemize}

All distributed copies must include the signed provenance ledger.

\section{Conclusion}
This README provides the structural and procedural foundation for maintaining
and distributing the ASTRO-SIM V1.0 monograph. By enforcing cryptographic
provenance, deterministic builds, and structured chapter integration, the
publication remains trustworthy, reproducible, and enterprise-grade.

